TinyStrata is an independent derivative of Niko1221/Strata.
Upstream: https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata
Base commit: 296b59d2f73c8f04a805df29c2fa97655adace78
Copyright (c) 2026 Niko1221 and the Strata contributors.
The upstream MIT license is preserved in LICENSE.

The Windows AMD HIP build/runtime route and GPU image-backend selection adapt
Niko1221/Strata at cbfd5b926b794b356195d3cb600191b0c3567540 (MIT), including
the WDDM memory-budget query and ROCm toolchain configuration. Existing AMD
kernel and HIP MMQ paths are retained; Windows hipBLAS error handling also
follows aflin/momoe at 47e5b2b2ab52982e105315bba2ac48ec75de01bf (MIT).
The CUDA-shaped HIP virtual-memory wrappers in include/strata/hip_compat/cuda.h
adapt VecSzn/PolyStrata at 51dc242725d9e64e791146f1d13133d5faedb0ce (MIT).

GGML-derived source and the pinned llama.cpp dependency are MIT licensed.
See third_party/ggml/LICENSE and third_party/ggml/VERSION.txt.
Existing file-level copyright and license notices remain in place.

The HTTP API server and tokenizer are adapted from the same upstream commit.

The image encoder in src/vision/tinystrata_vision.cpp adapts
tools/vision/strata_vision.cpp from the same upstream commit (MIT), using the
existing pinned llama.cpp mtmd and GGML libraries for image embeddings.

INT8 KV quantization and the dense prompt attention kernel are adapted from
aflin/momoe (https://github.com/aflin/momoe), an MIT-licensed Strata derivative.
Source commit: 47e5b2b2ab52982e105315bba2ac48ec75de01bf.
The dense kernel was introduced by Aaron Flin in commit
e5fd6d3acbe99f26ed7f179b6b35b8ec5343fb38. Original Strata copyright and MIT
license remain in LICENSE. Adaptations use TinyStrata's resident cache layout.
The HIP dense INT8 WMMA prompt kernel in src/qwen35/int8_attention_hip.cu
adapts the WMMA instruction/fragment and tiled dimension-group design from
Niko1221/Strata src/kernels/cuda/qsa_prompt_attn.cu at
5e8a4cca7d690ac60ca37eb09e7d0e010099ad6d (MIT), retaining TinyStrata's
residual compensation, dense causal cache layout and all visible tokens.
Native Q2_K/Q3_K expert dot helpers and Q2_K dequantization also adapt
src/kernels/cuda/iq_kernels.cu from the same MoMoE commit, with TinyStrata's
format dispatch and existing GGML block layouts. File-level attribution is retained.

Native FP8 attention instruction wrapper
include/strata/qwen35/fp8_mma.cuh adapts FlashInfer's
include/flashinfer/attention/sparse_mla_sm120/arch/mma_sm120.cuh at
38e6b8944fe8b6497d793ef21fbaadd797ea39d8 (https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer).
Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved.
BSD-3-Clause; full license and disclaimer retained in the adapted file and
third_party/licenses/FlashInfer-BSD-3-Clause.txt (include with binary distributions).
The surrounding dense scheduler is adapted from MoMoE, credited above.
The CUDA Qwen INT8 decode module adapts VecSzn/PolyStrata's
src/poly/fattn.cu at f472d85a30927301663401f7dc892e668578a90e (MIT), with
TinyStrata's per-64 KV layout and amplified FP16 residual compensation.
SageAttention d1a57a546c3d395b1ffcbeecc66d81db76f3b4b5 was consulted for
FP8 accumulation design; no SageAttention source is incorporated.

The optional Qwen3.6 hybrid CUDA Graph handoff adapts Strata's mapped-memory
notification, device wait and host graph-launch mechanisms from
src/core/session.cpp, src/kernels/cuda/elementwise.cu and
include/strata/core/host_graph_launch.hpp at the base commit listed above (MIT).
TinyStrata adds native-expert miss merging, multi-token replay service and a
persistent launch worker. Original copyright and MIT license are retained.

Qwen3.6 native-server consumed-history tracking follows Strata Flash-Next's
src/program/generate.cpp at the base commit listed above (MIT), recording the
whole committed speculative prefix before emitting a potentially shorter reply.

Additional Qwen3.6 small-row Q8 products, fused decode kernels and GDN prompt
optimizations adapt src/qwen35/q36_kernels.cuh and src/qwen35/q36_engine.cu from
Niko1221/Strata at 477ac13cbe8e582c20484871ce459d20d82df09d (MIT).
The optional AVX2 singleton IQ expert path adapts src/kernels/cpu/iq_avx2.cpp,
src/kernels/cpu/iq_avx2_rows.inl, src/kernels/cpu/native_expert.cpp and the
corresponding header from the same commit. Original copyright and MIT license
notices are retained.

The LFM2.5-24B-A2B engine, Expert cache/streaming, CPU worker pool,
LFM tokenizer and tool-call handling adapt the MIT-licensed PolyStrata project:
https://github.com/VecSzn/PolyStrata
Source commit: 26e4cb5df7996edfb5ff549a63b82d8581e1e658.
Only the LFM model path is incorporated. Expert omission is removed.
Original Strata and GGML copyright notices and licenses are preserved.

The Gemma 4 26B-A4B native engine, QAT assistant/MTP support and UTF-8-piece
tokenizer also adapt PolyStrata at commit
51dc242725d9e64e791146f1d13133d5faedb0ce (MIT), from src/poly/gemma4.*, the
shared engine/kernels and tools/strata_tokenizer.py. Only the Gemma model path
is added; all model-selected Experts are computed. The original MIT license
and file-level copyright notices are preserved.
Gemma's tool-call/thought-channel parsing and one-dimensional image embedding
format also adapt serve/frontend.py and tools/vision/strata_vision.cpp from
the same PolyStrata commit.

The optional browser UI in ui/web adapts serve/web from Niko1221/Strata at
5e8a4cca7d690ac60ca37eb09e7d0e010099ad6d (MIT). TinyStrata adds its terminal
theme, light mode, translations, API monitoring and live generation metrics.
The upstream MIT copyright and license are preserved in LICENSE.
Outfit fonts are distributed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; see
ui/web/fonts/OFL.txt. The offline KaTeX dependency is MIT licensed; see
ui/web/vendor/katex/LICENSE and ui/web/vendor/katex/PROVENANCE.json.
The offline Highlight.js syntax highlighter is BSD-3-Clause licensed; see
ui/web/vendor/highlight/LICENSE and ui/web/vendor/highlight/PROVENANCE.json.

The UI search/Python tool integration and SQLite history were independently
implemented after consulting Open WebUI at
f7ac7ee10962ddec0017f5c29b6740d9b9c5faca (https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui).
No Open WebUI source or branding assets are incorporated. Its distribution
license includes branding restrictions.
Browser Python uses the separately downloaded, pinned Pyodide 314.0.7 runtime
(MPL-2.0) and its dependencies. Runtime license and third-party notices are
included in ui/python-runtime-LICENSE.txt and ui/python-runtime-NOTICES.txt;
the UI copies them into the runtime cache during preparation.

Clover-35B-A3B-Preview support independently implements its published
bidirectional GDN, block coreset, and generation-control equations. References:
Diffuspace/Clover-35B-A3B-Preview at 4b0402b (Apache-2.0 model/custom code),
Maphist0/llama.cpp-pub dev-clover at 4838ffb0c8ade92f34d9157deea38d92758ab824
(llama.cpp PR #31306, MIT), and WilliamZR/sglang feature/clover-support at
2243dc6edb416073b60be0765904cabae9eb61cf (SGLang PR #46927, Apache-2.0).
Clover weights are downloaded separately from the official Diffuspace GGUF
repository and retain their Apache-2.0 model license and upstream Qwen attribution.

Gemma/LFM same-model conversation parking and bounded private spill files adapt
VecSzn/PolyStrata conversations.hpp at 6f279e9f4b82ce9c20a27df02b72601e690ce4ea
(MIT). Copyright (c) 2026 VecSzn and the PolyStrata contributors. TinyStrata adds
combined payload/metadata accounting, synchronous spill, opt-out handling,
image fingerprints and model-specific state/KV ordering.
Qwen/Clover prefill cancellation follows the complete-prefix retention approach
in aflin/momoe d5fe98dd5bb86bb67820160ff00d4afad853c93f (MIT), adapted to
TinyStrata's native GDN, MTP, image and staging lifetimes.
Gemma's configurable CUDA host upload chunk size follows the memory-sizing
approach in VecSzn/PolyStrata f2ce72b6720f4bfa722fd5ac3821789cb610f2c3 (MIT),
with TinyStrata's measured 256 MiB default and the existing two-buffer lifetime.

Native CPU Expert phase fusion adapts jesdga95/basalt
(https://github.com/jesdga95/basalt), src/kernels/cpu/pool.cpp and
include/basalt/kernels/cpu/pool.hpp at
bbf2f5bb783adc5ffe5b49043f82c9399313bb46 (MIT).
Copyright (c) 2026 Jesús Gulfo. The MIT license terms are preserved in LICENSE.
TinyStrata retains its per-row arithmetic, bounded scheduling and small-job
fallbacks.

The CUDA paired Q8_0 GDN projection schedule in src/qwen35/q36_pair.cuh was
independently implemented after consulting Basalt's docs/unified-kernel.md
at the same commit. TinyStrata retains its existing Q8_0 dot-product arithmetic
and uses one CUDA launch for the independent qkv and z projections.

The cooperative full GDN schedule in src/qwen35/q36_gdn_chain.cuh was
independently implemented after consulting Basalt's docs/unified-kernel.md
at bbf2f5bb783adc5ffe5b49043f82c9399313bb46 (MIT), credited above. TinyStrata
retains its existing projection, convolution and recurrent arithmetic.
The new header preserves the GGML authors' copyright, the pinned llama.cpp
3cf03257f219afbe7334045ff7c6a06ac68c627d attribution for Q6_K dot arithmetic,
and the complete MIT notice; see also third_party/ggml/LICENSE.

The eager hybrid CPU compact-result combine in src/qwen35/q36_engine.cu and
src/qwen35/q36_kernels.cuh was independently implemented after consulting
Basalt's docs/unified-kernel.md and src/kernels/cuda/dec_moe.cuh at
bbf2f5bb783adc5ffe5b49043f82c9399313bb46 (MIT), credited above. TinyStrata
retains its existing FP32 Expert results, weighted combine, normalization and
activation-quantization arithmetic; only result storage and scheduling change.
The manual empirical CPU-worker probe in benchmark/probe.py was independently
implemented after consulting Basalt's docs/probe.md at the same commit. It
measures candidate worker counts and reports recommendations without changing
saved model profiles or universal defaults.

Learned Expert ranking persistence and prompt-frequency seeding adapt Basalt's
src/core/expert_cache.cpp, src/program/serve/tier_profile.cpp and
src/program/serve/tiers.cpp at bbf2f5bb783adc5ffe5b49043f82c9399313bb46 (MIT),
credited above. TinyStrata binds rankings to the loaded model/layout identity,
uses current per-layer capacities, and collects completed prompt statistics
separately from accepted decode routing. No cached activations are serialized.

The Q5_0 GPU Expert-dot offset correction follows Niko1221/Strata commit
aa678f10d0e51ac17d301c75cbb6b80783437e8b (MIT), using the quantized
activation sum consistently with the integer products.
The resilient native/Vision UTF-8 subprocess readers follow jesdga95/basalt
commit 09f785308d88d1c8cdcb3711e8ca68bff8468d0f (MIT).
The explicit Qwen2 pre-tokenizer pattern and unsupported-pattern validation
follow aflin/momoe commit 7304c605a65d30484294946c079b733dbe18179d (MIT).
The bounded closing-tag lookahead and final-boundary handling for streamed
tool arguments adapt Niko1221/Strata commits
49b880c01f55a248d0485b6cd244ae053191d928 and
3bbf0f399e2a1b3d38642eca4342721fc7994201 (MIT), preserving literal closing
tags inside tool argument values.

Packed-register byte extraction in src/kernels/cuda/iq_kernels.cu and
include/strata/kernels/packed_byte.hpp adapts jesdga95/basalt commits
5bdb6c61ff99247899515c378856f49728e4a69b,
f83263da69e4e03145da3006e145b820836a6db3 and
dbc515818ec5b74014efbbc69e4c42958a03414d (MIT), credited above.
The CPU pool's one-time stall-clock arming adapts Basalt commit
2c4a0eb678265f0c5a473cdabfc808577dcaa6f5 (MIT). TinyStrata retains
its atomic claim/completion protocol, park waits, arithmetic and stall diagnostics.
